IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epd-nouns`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), consolidated version of 19.12.2009: Articles 7 and 8.
-- LAYER 1. Itemised billing (Art 7) and line identification (Art 8).
-- A rule named "... must offer ..." says whether the duty binds on the stated facts; a rule named "... duty ... is met" says
-- whether it was met once it binds. JUST TRUE = the text says yes, JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words, NOTHING =
-- not covered (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").

§ `Article 7 -- itemised billing`

-- src:91 | Subscribers shall have the right to receive non-itemised bills.
@ref Art 7(1) (src:91) row:A7(1)
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(1) the subscriber has the right to receive non-itemised bills` MEANS
    IF `the person is a subscriber`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given to subscribers; the sentence is silent on anyone else
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:92 | Member States shall apply national provisions in order to reconcile the rights of subscribers receiving itemised bills with the right to privacy of calling users and called subscribers
@ref Art 7(2) first limb (src:92) row:A7(2)
GIVEN `the subscriber receives itemised bills` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(2) the Member State must apply national provisions to reconcile the rights of subscribers receiving itemised bills with the privacy of calling users and called subscribers` MEANS
    IF `the subscriber receives itemised bills`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for the rights of subscribers receiving itemised bills
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:92 | for example by ensuring that sufficient alternative privacy enhancing methods of communications or payments are available to such users and subscribers.
@ref Art 7(2) example (src:92) row:A7(2)
GIVEN `sufficient alternative privacy enhancing methods of communications or payments are available to the calling users and called subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 7(2) the national provisions reconcile the rights in the way the text gives as an example` MEANS
    IF `sufficient alternative privacy enhancing methods of communications or payments are available to the calling users and called subscribers`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "for example" gives one way of reconciling and does not close the list
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Article 8 -- presentation and restriction of calling and connected line identification`

§§ `Art 8(1) -- the calling user and the calling subscriber`

-- src:95 | Where presentation of calling line identification is offered, the service provider must offer the calling user the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge, of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification on a per-call basis.
@ref Art 8(1) first sentence (src:95) row:A8(1).s1
GIVEN `presentation of calling line identification is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) first sentence the service provider must offer the calling user the possibility of preventing the presentation on a per-call basis` MEANS
    IF `presentation of calling line identification is offered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where presentation of calling line identification is offered" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the provider offers the calling user the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility is on a per-call basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility uses a simple means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility is free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) first sentence the service provider's duty to the calling user is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider offers the calling user the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification`
       AND `the possibility is on a per-call basis`
       AND `the possibility uses a simple means`
       AND `the possibility is free of charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must offer the calling user the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge, of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification on a per-call basis"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:95 | The calling subscriber must have this possibility on a per-line basis.
@ref Art 8(1) second sentence (src:95) row:A8(1).s2
GIVEN `presentation of calling line identification is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) second sentence the calling subscriber must have the possibility on a per-line basis` MEANS
    IF `presentation of calling line identification is offered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where presentation of calling line identification is offered" in the first sentence, which "this possibility" of the second carries over -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6, F24: "this possibility" is read as carrying the first sentence's "where" over
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the calling subscriber has the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility is on a per-line basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) second sentence the calling subscriber's possibility on a per-line basis is met` MEANS
    IF `the calling subscriber has the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification` AND `the possibility is on a per-line basis`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The calling subscriber must have this possibility on a per-line basis"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 8(2) -- the called subscriber and incoming calls`

-- src:96 | Where presentation of calling line identification is offered, the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge for reasonable use of this function, of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification of incoming calls.
@ref Art 8(2) (src:96) row:A8(2)
GIVEN `presentation of calling line identification is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(2) the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification of incoming calls` MEANS
    IF `presentation of calling line identification is offered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where presentation of calling line identification is offered" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification of incoming calls` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility uses a simple means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of this function is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility is free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(2) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must offer the called subscriber the possibility, using a simple means"
        IF (NOT `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification of incoming calls`) OR (NOT `the possibility uses a simple means`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "free of charge for reasonable use of this function" -- for use that is not reasonable the sentence does not say the possibility must be free
        IF NOT `the use of this function is reasonable` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "free of charge for reasonable use of this function"
        IF NOT `the possibility is free of charge` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Art 8(3) -- rejecting incoming calls whose identification was prevented`

-- src:97 | Where presentation of calling line identification is offered and where the calling line identification is presented prior to the call being established, the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility, using a simple means, of rejecting incoming calls where the presentation of the calling line identification has been prevented by the calling user or subscriber.
@ref Art 8(3) (src:97) row:A8(3)
GIVEN `presentation of calling line identification is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the calling line identification is presented prior to the call being established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(3) the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility of rejecting incoming calls whose presentation was prevented` MEANS
    IF `presentation of calling line identification is offered` AND `the calling line identification is presented prior to the call being established`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where presentation of calling line identification is offered and where the calling line identification is presented prior to the call being established" -- two "where" conditions, one failing (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of rejecting incoming calls where the presentation of the calling line identification has been prevented by the calling user or subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility uses a simple means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(3) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of rejecting incoming calls where the presentation of the calling line identification has been prevented by the calling user or subscriber` AND `the possibility uses a simple means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must offer the called subscriber the possibility, using a simple means, of rejecting incoming calls"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 8(4) -- connected line identification`

-- src:98 | Where presentation of connected line identification is offered, the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge, of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification to the calling user.
@ref Art 8(4) (src:98) row:A8(4)
GIVEN `presentation of connected line identification is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(4) the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification` MEANS
    IF `presentation of connected line identification is offered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where presentation of connected line identification is offered" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification to the calling user` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility uses a simple means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possibility is free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(4) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification to the calling user` AND `the possibility uses a simple means` AND `the possibility is free of charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must offer the called subscriber the possibility, using a simple means and free of charge, of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification to the calling user"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 8(5) -- third countries`

-- src:99 | Paragraph 1 shall also apply with regard to calls to third countries originating in the Community.
@ref Art 8(5) first sentence (src:99) row:A8(5).s1
GIVEN `the call is to a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the call originates in the Community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(5) first sentence paragraph 1 applies to the call` MEANS
    IF `the call is to a third country` AND `the call originates in the Community`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "also apply" extends paragraph 1 to calls to third countries originating in the Community and says nothing of other calls
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:99 | Paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 shall also apply to incoming calls originating in third countries.
@ref Art 8(5) second sentence (src:99) row:A8(5).s2
GIVEN `the call is an incoming call` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the call originates in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(5) second sentence paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 apply to the call` MEANS
    IF `the call is an incoming call` AND `the call originates in a third country`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "also apply" extends paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 to incoming calls originating in third countries and says nothing of other calls
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Art 8(6) -- telling the public`

-- src:100 | Member States shall ensure that where presentation of calling and/or connected line identification is offered, the providers of publicly available electronic communications services inform the public thereof and of the possibilities set out in paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 4.
@ref Art 8(6) (src:100) row:A8(6)
GIVEN `presentation of calling line identification or connected line identification is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(6) the provider must inform the public of the line identification and of the possibilities` MEANS
    IF `presentation of calling line identification or connected line identification is offered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where presentation of calling and/or connected line identification is offered" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the provider informs the public that presentation is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider informs the public of the possibilities set out in paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(6) the provider's duty to inform the public is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider informs the public that presentation is offered` AND `the provider informs the public of the possibilities set out in paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 4`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "inform the public thereof and of the possibilities set out in paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 4"
    ELSE JUST FALSE
